# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#  HazardNet — environment template (local development / self-host)
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
#
#  Copy to `.env` (gitignored) and fill in:
#
#      cp .env.example .env
#
#  ⚠️  PLACEHOLDERS ONLY. A previous revision of this file shipped live
#      credentials; treat those values as leaked and rotate them — see
#      docs/ops/owner-actions.md for the rotation checklist.
#
#  This file is read by BOTH:
#    • the Node backend   — backend/server.js (dotenv)
#    • the Vite client build — frontend/vite.config.ts loads the *repository
#      root* env (`loadEnv(mode, '..', '')`) and injects a fixed set of values
#      into the bundle. That is why the Supabase/frontend keys in §7 live here
#      and not in frontend/.env — see §7 and frontend/.env.example.
#
#  Vars marked REQUIRED fail closed when unset: the feature refuses to run
#  rather than silently allowing traffic. Vars marked (optional) have the
#  documented default and can be left blank.
# ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════


# ── 1. Runtime / process ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Node environment. `production` switches on HSTS and strict CSP behaviour
# (backend/middleware/securityHeaders.js) and turns off the dev-only
# permissive CORS fallback (backend/middleware/cors.js).
NODE_ENV=development

# Port the backend listens on. Default 3000; it binds 0.0.0.0.
PORT=3000

# Vercel platform marker — set for you by Vercel's build/runtime, not by hand.
# `production` is treated exactly like NODE_ENV=production.
VERCEL_ENV=


# ── 2. Security ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED by the four key-guarded write endpoints. Verified with a
# constant-time compare (backend/utils/apiKeyAuth.js):
#   backend  POST /api/v1/forecasts/update     (CSV ingest)
#            POST /api/push/send               (broadcast)
#   serverless (Vercel functions)
#            POST /api/ingest  and  POST /api/forecasts
#
# LEAVE EMPTY UNTIL YOU SET A REAL ONE: when unset those endpoints answer 503
# "Service authentication is not configured" — fail closed. A placeholder
# literal here would instead be accepted as a valid key by anyone who reads
# this file.
#   Generate:  openssl rand -hex 32
BACKEND_API_KEY=

# Comma-separated list of browser origins allowed to call the API.
# REQUIRED in production: when unset there, cross-origin browser requests are
# REJECTED (fail closed). The localhost loopbacks are always allowed and need
# no entry here. Trailing slashes are not normalised — list the bare origin.
FRONTEND_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000

# Set to `true` to ENFORCE the Content-Security-Policy. Left `false` (default)
# the policy is served in report-only style, so it cannot break the app while
# you tune the allowlist. Turn on in production once verified.
CSP_ENFORCE=false


# ── 3. Forecast store ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Which forecast backend to read. `supabase` = Supabase Postgres (ADR 0002
# cutover, the production path); anything else falls back to `firestore`
# (the legacy AI-Studio applet database).
FORECAST_STORE=firestore

# REQUIRED when FORECAST_STORE=supabase — the Postgres connection string.
# The backend throws at startup without it. Use the pooler URL (port 6543)
# for serverless runtimes; SUPABASE_DB_URL holds the same value for CI.
#   Shape:  postgresql://USER:PASSWORD@HOST:6543/postgres
DATABASE_URL=

# `true` connects with TLS (rejectUnauthorized:false, for Supabase's pooler).
SUPABASE_SSL=true

# (optional) Supabase project JWT secret (HS256). Never blocks a request:
# a valid token raises that user's AI rate limit from 10 to 60 req/min.
# Leave blank and anonymous traffic still works, just at the tight lane.
SUPABASE_JWT_SECRET=

# (optional) Only read by scripts/migrate-firestore-to-supabase.mjs, which is
# dry-run unless this is exactly `RUN`. Do not set this in a normal runtime.
FIRESTORE_TO_SUPABASE_MIGRATION=

# (optional) Kaggle dataset that /api/v1/forecasts/metadata reports as the
# data source. Default: ashifahmedshuvo/hazardnet-weekly-forecasts
KAGGLE_DATASET=


# ── 4. AI providers ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# REQUIRED for the advisory/chat/agent routes. The fallback engine tries the
# backup key and the alternatives below in order, so a single provider outage
# degrades rather than breaks.
GEMINI_API_KEY=
GEMINI_API_KEY_BACKUP=
OPENROUTER_API_KEY=
GROQ_API_KEY=
HUGGINGFACE_API_KEY=


# ── 5. Web push (VAPID) ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Generate ONE pair per environment:   npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
# VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY is the server identity and must match the client's
# VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY (frontend/.env). VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY is optional in
# development — without it the server generates an ephemeral pair, which
# invalidates every existing subscription on restart. Always set it in
# production.
#   Generate:  npx web-push generate-vapid-keys
VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY=
VAPID_PRIVATE_KEY=
WEB_PUSH_CONTACT=mailto:shuvo.1807016@bau.edu.bd


# ── 6. Tooling / diagnostics ───────────────────────────────────────────────
# (optional) Base URL probed by scripts/bench-predict.mjs.
# Default: http://127.0.0.1:3001
BENCH_URL=


# ── 7. Values injected into the built client (read by Vite from THIS file) ─
#
# ⚠️  READ THIS BEFORE EDITING frontend/.env
#
# frontend/vite.config.ts has an explicit `define` block that textually
# substitutes these names at build time, sourced from loadEnv(mode, '..') —
# i.e. from THIS file at the repository root. A value set in
# frontend/.env is therefore IGNORED for exactly these keys (verified by
# build: a decoy VITE_SUPABASE_URL in frontend/.env never reaches the bundle).
#
# Both a canonical and an alias name work; the first one set wins.
#
# Supabase project URL          (→ import.meta.env.VITE_SUPABASE_URL)
#   alias: SUPABASE_URL
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
SUPABASE_URL=

# Supabase publishable/anon key (→ VITE_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY)
#   aliases: SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY, NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
SUPABASE_PUBLISHABLE_KEY=
NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Where Supabase should send users back after email/OAuth confirmation
# (→ VITE_SUPABASE_REDIRECT_URL). Falls back at runtime to
# `${window.location.origin}/auth/callback`.
NEXT_PUBLIC_DEV_SUPABASE_REDIRECT_URL=

# Vercel Web Analytics gate. Leave blank: the build enables the loader only
# when Vercel itself is building (VERCEL=1), because `/_vercel/insights/`
# is a Vercel-only route — see frontend/src/lib/vercelAnalytics.ts.
# `true` forces it on, `false` forces it off.
VITE_VERCEL_ANALYTICS=


# ── 8. GitHub Actions repository secrets (NOT for this file) ───────────────
#
# These are configured in GitHub → Settings → Secrets and variables →
# Actions. They are documented here only so the full set is discoverable in
# one place; putting them in `.env` has no effect.
#
#   BACKEND_API_KEY      fail-fast check + the value the API expects (§2)
#   SUPABASE_DB_URL      Postgres URL for the migration/verify scripts
#   GEMINI_API_KEY       advisory generation in the data pipelines
#   KAGGLE_USERNAME      Kaggle API auth for the forecast pipelines
#   KAGGLE_KEY           Kaggle API key — NOT "KAGGLE_API_TOKEN", which is not
#                        read by anything (an earlier revision of this file
#                        documented the wrong name)
#   CODECOV_TOKEN        coverage uploads (optional; upload is non-blocking)
#   GITHUB_TOKEN         provided automatically by Actions — never set it
#
# NOT required: VERCEL_TOKEN / VERCEL_ORG_ID / VERCEL_PROJECT_ID. CI no longer
# deploys to Vercel — the Git integration does that. Those secrets are unused
# and can be deleted (docs/audits/2026-09-14-vercel-deploy-403-project-unresolved.md).
#
# The release templates (.github/workflow-templates/) additionally read
# PYPI_API_TOKEN, NPM_AUTH_TOKEN, ANDROID_KEYSTORE_* and CODE_SIGNING_CERT_*
# when those pipelines are adopted.
